&& HELP_META_HARVEST_EXPORT_v1.dts
&&
&& LANE: MAINT (maintenance/SDLC) -- the manualgen HELP/META harvest feeder.
&&   BBOX only TEACHES this lane (data -> process -> information out); MAINT is
&&   the maintenance EXECUTION surface it belongs to. MAINT is read-only first
&&   wave and states "PowerShell is MDO scaffolding only; the permanent
&&   maintenance app is native C++" -- so this script IS that scaffolding,
&&   standing in until a native MAINT harvest verb adopts it.
&&
&& Re-export the LIVE HELP + META tables to CSV so the manualgen harvest can be
&& refreshed from CURRENT runtime evidence. This is the "feeder" the manualgen
&& system needs and that was mostly never committed: the harvest workspace
&& (docs\manuals\developer\manualgen\harvested) is regenerable, gitignored
&& EXHAUST, and only ONE per-table export (SYSCMD_EXPORT_MIRROR_v1) existed.
&&
&& DIRECTION, EMPHATICALLY: the table is authority; the CSV is its readable
&& shadow. This is an EXPORT, never an import.
&&
&& COVERS the 10 CURRENT tables:
&&   6 HELP_*  from data\help    -> COMMANDS, CMD_ARGS, HELP_ARTIFACTS,
&&                                  HELP_LINE, HELP_SECTION, HELP_TOPIC
&&   4 META_*  from data\metadata-> SYSCMD, SYSFUNC, SYSARGS, SYSSUBCMD
&&
&& DELIBERATELY OMITTED (do NOT launder stale data into the manual):
&&   META_SYSENTVAR, META_SYSFLDDIC, META_SYSHELP, META_SYSMSG.
&&   These sources are stale May seeds/stubs; the live message catalog is the
&&   separate SYSTEM_MESSAGES / SYSTEM_MESSAGE_TEXT pair, and DDICT is
&&   PLANNED-only. The companion .ps1 carries the prior May CSVs forward
&&   LABELLED CARRIED_STALE so manualgen still sees 14 files, without pretending
&&   they are current. They stay owed until their sources are refreshed.
&&
&& MUTATION: writes 10 files under DATA\tmp. Touches no table, index, or LMDB.
&&   The companion HELP_META_HARVEST_EXPORT_v1.ps1 promotes + stamps + hashes.
&&
&& PATH PROTOCOL: SETPATH DBF <dir>, then a BARE table name. Slashed relative
&&   paths (tmp/...) resolve against the DATA root, not the DBF slot.
&&
&& Run via the companion .ps1, or directly:
&&   ./datarun.ps1 -CommandLines 'DOTSCRIPT <abs path to this file>'

SET TALK OFF

; ===== HELP lane (data\help) -> HELP_*.csv =====
SETPATH DBF help
WORKSPACE CLOSE

USE COMMANDS
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_COMMANDS.csv CSV

USE CMD_ARGS
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_CMD_ARGS.csv CSV

USE HELP_ARTIFACTS
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_HELP_ARTIFACTS.csv CSV

USE HELP_LINE
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_HELP_LINE.csv CSV

USE HELP_SECTION
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_HELP_SECTION.csv CSV

USE HELP_TOPIC
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/HELP_HELP_TOPIC.csv CSV

; ===== META lane (data\metadata) -> META_*.csv (the CURRENT four only) =====
SETPATH DBF metadata
WORKSPACE CLOSE

USE SYSCMD
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/META_SYSCMD.csv CSV

USE SYSFUNC
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/META_SYSFUNC.csv CSV

USE SYSARGS
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/META_SYSARGS.csv CSV

USE SYSSUBCMD
COUNT
EXPORT TO tmp/META_SYSSUBCMD.csv CSV

QUIT
